          "text": "The pattern indexes as **\u03b2-quartz-type TiO\u2082**, with a hexagonal cell:\n\n- \\(a=b \\approx 5.6166\\) \u00c5\n- \\(c \\approx 6.1273\\) \u00c5\n- \\(Z=3\\)\n- probable space group **P6\u208222** (No. 180)\n\nRepresentative indexing is: 18.23\u00b0 (100), 23.33\u00b0 (101), 31.84\u00b0 (110), 34.58\u00b0 (102), 35.13\u00b0 (111), 36.93\u00b0 (200), 39.85\u00b0 (201), 43.69\u00b0 (112), 44.32\u00b0 (003), 47.71\u00b0 (202), and 48.29\u00b0 (103). The absence of 001/002 and presence of 003 supports the screw-axis quartz structure.\n\n### Primary CIF\n\n```cif\ndata_TiO2_beta_quartz_P6222\n_audit_creation_method              'Indexed and modeled from powder XRD'\n_chemical_name_common               'beta-quartz-type titanium dioxide'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'TiO2'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'O2 Ti'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               3\n\n_cell_length_a                      5.6166\n_cell_length_b                      5.6166\n_cell_length_c                      6.1273\n_cell_angle_alpha                   90\n_cell_angle_beta                    90\n_cell_angle_gamma                   120\n_cell_volume                        167.397\n\n_space_group_crystal_system         hexagonal\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt           'P 62 2 2'\n_space_group_IT_number              180\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type              'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\nTi1  Ti  3  0.500000  0.000000  0.000000  1.0\nO1   O   6  0.414100  0.207050  0.166667  1.0\n```\n\nThe oxygen coordinate is the quartz-framework parameterization \\((2u,u,1/6)\\), with \\(u\\approx0.20705\\).\n\n### Indistinguishable enantiomorph\n\nOrdinary powder diffraction cannot distinguish **P6\u208222** from its opposite-handed enantiomorph **P6\u208422** (No. 181). The corresponding inverted model is:\n\n```cif\ndata_TiO2_beta_quartz_P6422\n_audit_creation_method              'Enantiomorph of the powder-XRD solution'\n_chemical_name_common               'beta-quartz-type titanium dioxide, opposite hand'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'TiO2'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'O2 Ti'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               3\n\n_cell_length_a                      5.6166\n_cell_length_b                      5.6166\n_cell_length_c                      6.1273\n_cell_angle_alpha                   90\n_cell_angle_beta                    90\n_cell_angle_gamma                   120\n_cell_volume                        167.397\n\n_space_group_crystal_system         hexagonal\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt           'P 64 2 2'\n_space_group_IT_number              181\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type              'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\nTi1  Ti  3  0.500000  0.000000  0.000000  1.0\nO1   O   6  0.585900  0.792950  0.833333  1.0\n```\n\nNo rutile, anatase, or brookite alternative accounts for the low-angle 18.23\u00b0 and 23.33\u00b0 reflections or the complete peak sequence.",
